    def clearPSDDefinitions(self):
        r"""
        Clears PSD definition data.

        PSD stands for pose space deformation. It describes how multiple expressions are combined and which corrections have to
        be applied to specific expression combinations in order to get correct resulting shape.
        For example, expressions jawOpen and cornerPuller are combined into expression openSmile.
        Expression openSmile_cmx represents actual combination when both jawOpen and cornerPuller expressions are activated.
        (openSmile_cmx = jawOpen + cornerPuller)
        However, simple expression combinations don't always look how we would like them to. That is why we introduce
        openSmile_tgt, a target expression that represents how that combination should actually look like. Finally, we
        calculate corrective expression openSmile_cor by subtracting openSmile_cmx from openSmile_tgt. (openSmile_cor =
        openSmile_tgt - openSmile_cmx) For each PSD definition there exists a corresponding PSD net. In this example, the
        corresponding PSD net makes sure that each time both jawOpen and cornerPuller are activated, it activates openSmile_cor
        as well, making sure that openSmile looks correctly. Formula: openSmile_tgt = jawOpen + cornerPuller + openSmile_cor
        See also: PSDNetReader
        """
        return _py3rdf6_4_1.PSDDefinitionWriter_clearPSDDefinitions(self)

